// The bow (the archer): arrows fly where you aim (the crosshair). Light is drawn while you hold it: a
// tap looses a weak quick arrow, a full draw (0.6 s) one three times as hard and
// faster ("charge": held at frame "at" for up to "frames", "damage" and "speed" at full draw; "hold":
// a full draw waits for you to let go).
// Heavy draws a power shot that hits hard and breaks poise. It keeps you moving while you
// shoot, but up close it has nothing: keep your distance, roll away and shoot again.
// A "projectile" leaves on the attack's first active frame; "count" and "spread" fan several out.
// The swings hold the bow upright (pitch 90: the string to you, the belly to the target) and let it
// kick forward a little as the arrow leaves. followArm: while it shoots, the bow is held where the arm
// points (out at the shoulder), not at the hip. view: where it is held in first person (right, up,
// forward from the eye; tuning firstPerson.weapon if not set): further out than the others, as it is tall.
// viewTilt: in first person it leans this many degrees, the top to the left.
